{"agent":"fx-dupe-research-task","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new guard does not actually enforce the knob’s documented promise that `Identical text still asks` for a research-note/task pair. The function’s identical-flag check at the top of `_asks` returns `True` only for the same-kind identical duplicate case; a research add whose title/body is byte-for-byte identical to an existing task is a different-kind match, so it will not carry the `identical` flag. With `research_task_asks=False`, `_note_vs_work(\"research\", \"task\")` is `True`, the added `and \"identical\" not in c.flags` is also `True`, and `_asks` returns `False`, so `assess` reports `show` instead of `ask`. For example, adding `{\"kind\": \"research\", \"title\": \"\", \"body\": \"exact same body\"}` against an existing `{\"kind\": \"task\", \"title\": \"\", \"body\": \"exact same body\"}` will be shown, contrary to “Identical text still asks.”","digest":"1eb68f6c8e0aadf2","location":"ddflow/services/similar.py:_asks","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/similar.py:_asks"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":4473,"diff_sha":"ad9356130bff6fcaea4039828df9affea38ac2840f362bd4071dd67d8d1f73b2","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":353.9,"excluded_bytes":1177503,"excluded_files":2,"excluded_paths":["README.md","tests/test_uc_surf_setup_ops_transcript.json"],"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"48218c5724384881","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-dupe-research-vs-task.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261021T141211Z-b9cfadb3.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"bf05df9af0bab7d32b8f99f51c79e0541e3bc518","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v